\f1\fs22 Sarah heard a sound like the snap of fingers\'97then a silence so deep it seemed the world had blinked to black.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Less than a second later, Tony\'92s vision flickered back. The hall wall cracked and toppled, as if smashed in by a runaway truck. Sarah yanked Tony to the floor as the blunt blast-wave receded and left his ears ringing, the ceiling wrenching loose above them. Splinters, rubble, chunks of plaster rained down. Sarah grunted, disappearing into the falling grey; heavy dust coated her hair and stuck in new blood.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony huddled as the debris pummelled down, too late to save anyone but himself.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He risked a look: the fallen wall, caught by another that just bore the weight of whatever was above, had left a tight, slanted crawlspace around them. It wouldn\'92t hold long.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah!\'94 Tony slapped her cheeks. Nothing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clatter faded, giving way to moans and distant shrieks. Crouching under the makeshift lean-to, Tony wriggled his arms under Sarah\'92s and dragged her backwards, hoping the club\'92s lobby hadn\'92t vanished in the explosion.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>There was a dull whomp, like a gas oven lighting, and an orange flare curled past\'97swirling fire licked at the spill of dust around Tony. Screams rose and filled the air. Some of them were his.\

